note: The best group: the X with the highest total Y, where X is a field of the rows, and the top N groups.
a purchase has a store, a category and an amount.
let purchases be a list of a new purchase with store "Nobu", category "food", amount 96,
    a new purchase with store "Apple", category "tech", amount 249,
    a new purchase with store "Nobu", category "food", amount 200,
    a new purchase with store "Whole Foods", category "food", amount 84,
    a new purchase with store "Whole Foods", category "food", amount 312.
say "Top store:", the store with the highest total amount.
say the store with the lowest total amount.
say the store with the highest average amount, the category with the highest number of purchases.
say the top 2 stores by total amount.
say the lowest 1 stores by total amount of purchases.
say the store with the highest median amount of purchases.
say the category with the highest total amount of the purchases whose amount is over 100.
let n be 3.
say the top n stores by average amount.
say the lowest 2 categories by number of purchases.
